        "original_id": "9fad4a74-17c9-5d45-b263-7576881211cc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Jackson, Joe Strummer, John Graham Mellor\n- Organizations: the Clash\n- Products: Moonwalk, The Essential Clash\n- Topics: music, autobiography, punk rock\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Jackson was born as Michael Joseph Jackson on August 29, 1958, and he was an American singer, songwriter, and dancer.\n- Joe Strummer was born as John Graham Mellor on August 21, 1952, and he was an English musician, singer, actor, and songwriter.\n- The Clash was a punk rock band formed in 1976 as part of the original wave of British punk.\n- Joe Strummer was a co-founder, lyricist, rhythm guitarist, and lead vocalist of the Clash.\n- Moonwalk is a 1988 autobiography written by American recording artist Michael Jackson.\n- Joe Strummer died on December 22, 2002, during the compilation of The Essential Clash.\n- The album The Essential Clash is dedicated to Joe Strummer.\n- Michael Jackson died on June 25, 2009.",
